Package: openreadout
Type: Package
Title: Read Raw Laboratory Instrument Files Without Vendor Software
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Richard", "Zimring", email = "openreadout@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("The OpenReadout Authors", role = "cph"))
Description: Reads raw files from laboratory instruments such as microscopes,
    mass spectrometers and plate readers into R arrays and data frames, and
    exports them to open formats. The readers are the 'OpenReadout' Rust
    library, which is bundled with the package and needs no vendor software.
License: MIT + file LICENSE | Apache License (== 2.0)
URL: https://github.com/openreadout/openreadout
BugReports: https://github.com/openreadout/openreadout/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports: jsonlite
Suggests: arrow, digest, testthat (>= 3.0.0), tibble, withr
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc >= 1.91, xz
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
